#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports-dev.md:137
msgid ""
"The first three are the diagnosis: running them in order tells you *which"
" of the three segments* is wrong, which is a much smaller question than "
"\"the page is wrong\". The line-set modes answer the question that comes "
"before writing a selection at all:"
msgstr ""
"Os três primeiros são o diagnóstico: rodá-los em ordem diz *qual dos três"
" segmentos* está errado, que é pergunta muito menor do que \"a página "
"está errada\". Os modos de conjunto de linhas respondem à pergunta que "
"vem antes mesmo de escrever uma seleção:"

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports-dev.md:145
msgid ""
"`--page-type` matters even in the pipeline modes: it is what decides "
"which pipeline the page is fed through, so inspecting a page as the wrong"
" class shows you a correct answer to the wrong question."
msgstr ""
"O `--page-type` conta mesmo nos modos de pipeline: é ele que decide por "
"qual pipeline a página passa, então inspecionar uma página como a classe "
"errada mostra uma resposta correta à pergunta errada."

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports-dev.md:149
msgid "`probe` — ready-made questions to ask a document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports-dev.md:151
msgid ""
"Before a format exists there is nothing for `inspect-page` to run, and "
"the first questions are about the documents themselves: *what kind of "
"report is this*, *where are the totals*, *who manages the investments*. A"
" **probe** is a small script that asks one such question of one or more "
"PDFs and prints what it found, with pages, positions and fonts. A few "
"ship with the tool."
