#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports-dev.md:182
msgid ""
"**What a probe answers is a lead, not a result.** Probes are deliberately"
" rough: they take the first match, and the first match in a financial "
"report is often the table of contents. A probe that says `-` has not "
"proven that something is absent, only that it did not find it the way it "
"looks; and a probe that finds a value has found *a* value, which the page"
" still has to confirm. Their use is to tell you, across several reports "
"of the same format at once, whether an anchor holds — which is the "
"question that decides whether a format can be written at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/freeports-dev.md:189
msgid ""
"**The tool's own options may appear anywhere**, before or after the "
"probe's name; everything else after the name goes to the probe, in its "
"order. The documents start at the first word that names an existing file "
"or directory, and nothing may follow them."
msgstr ""

